    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d617">

                <pb facs="0602" n="1336" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1336"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-11-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>At Beirut and Alexandretta to interchange, and one always at Mersine.
                    Missionaries report that the presence of <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi>
                    prevented massacre at Adana. They beg that a light-armed dispatch bark will be
                    kept at Constantinople. Every great power has one here. A revolution is
                    preparing in Macedonia. Turkish garrison of 400 killed and captured at
                    Zeitoun.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
